HumanDoc:
  docs/skills/cross-cutting/architecture/clean-architecture.md

Evidence:
  - Clean Architecture by Robert C. Martin
  - Hexagonal Architecture
  - Production experience

Rules:
  [C1] Dependencies MUST point inward.
  [C2] Entities MUST NOT depend on frameworks.
  [C3] Use cases MUST NOT depend on UI or database.
  [C4] Interface adapters MUST convert data formats.
  [C5] Frameworks and drivers are external.
  [C6] Use dependency inversion principle.
  [C7] Test inner layers without outer layers.
  [C8] Keep business logic independent.

Pros:
  - Testable
  - Maintainable
  - Framework independent

Cons:
  - More files
  - Initial complexity
  - Over-abstraction risk

Alternatives:
  - DDD
  - Modular monolith
  - Hexagonal architecture

State: +

